{
  "pdf_filename": "Feijoo_DarkIR_Robust_Low-Light_Image_Restoration_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf",
  "title": "DarkIR: Robust Low-Light Image Restoration (Phục hồi hình ảnh thiếu sáng mạnh mẽ)",
  "total_pages": 11,
  "total_batches": 3,
  "figures": [
    {
      "num": 1,
      "page": 1,
      "filename": "figure_01.png",
      "rel_path": "figures/figure_01.png",
      "width": 1282,
      "height": 920,
      "caption": "Figure 1. Previous Low-light Image Enhancement (LLIE) and restoration methods are not robust to blur and illumination changes. Our\nmulti-task model is able to restore real low-light images under varying illumination, noise and blur conditions. Zoom-in to see details."
    },
    {
      "num": 2,
      "page": 3,
      "filename": "figure_02.png",
      "rel_path": "figures/figure_02.png",
      "width": 1374,
      "height": 534,
      "caption": "Figure 2. General diagram of DarkIR. The neural network follows an encoder-decoder architecture. We use different blocks for encoding\nand decoding that follow the Metaformer structure [56]. The encoder focuses on the low-light illumination issues using Fourier information.\nThus, the encoder produces a low-resolution reconstructed image ˆx↓8 with corrected illumination. The decoder focuses on upscaling and\nreducing the blur using the prior illumination-enhanced encoded features. To achieve this, the decoder uses large receptive field spatial\nattention. This design allows our lightweight model to have less parameters and FLOPs than previous methods."
    },
    {
      "num": 3,
      "page": 5,
      "filename": "figure_03.png",
      "rel_path": "figures/figure_03.png",
      "width": 1396,
      "height": 646,
      "caption": "Figure 3. Qualitative comparisons on the LOLBlur dataset (synthetic samples from the testset)."
    },
    {
      "num": 4,
      "page": 6,
      "filename": "figure_04.png",
      "rel_path": "figures/figure_04.png",
      "width": 1386,
      "height": 720,
      "caption": "Figure 4. Additional visual comparisons on the LOLBlur [65] dataset with 2-step pipelines. DarkIR generates much sharper images with\nvisually pleasing results. (Zoom in for best view)."
    },
    {
      "num": 5,
      "page": 7,
      "filename": "figure_05.png",
      "rel_path": "figures/figure_05.png",
      "width": 1378,
      "height": 231,
      "caption": "Figure 5. Qualitative results on the real-world dataset LSRW-Huawei [19]. We provide more samples in the supplementary."
    },
    {
      "num": 6,
      "page": 7,
